### User Executions & Environment Settings
# Import WAYLAND_DISPLAY/SWAYSOCK into the systemd --user manager's own
# environment FIRST -- it's separate from sway's process environment, and
# systemd --user services (like swayidle.service right below) can't reach
# the compositor at all until this has run. Learned this one from a real
# failure: swayidle.service crash-looped with "Unable to connect to the
# compositor" because this used to run near the end of this file, after
# the swayidle restart below had already fired.
#
# sway-session.sh does that, starts sway-session.target (binds
# graphical-session.target) and stops it when sway shuts down, so the
# PartOf=graphical-session.target units stop with sway. The user manager
# lingers across logout; without this they crash-looped with no compositor
# (xdg-desktop-portal-luminous hit its start limit after a logout).
exec ~/.local/bin/sway-session.sh

# Everything that runs for the whole session is a systemd user unit that
# sway-session.sh starts right after importing WAYLAND_DISPLAY (so none can
# race that import), restarts on a crash, and logs to the journal under its
# own name (`vayu-logs <name>`): waybar, vyom (panels and notifications), nada (music),
# bar-events (capsule refreshes), ekatva (phone), the audio idle
# inhibitor, lock-before-sleep, batsignal, and the clipboard history
# (cliphist@text, cliphist@image). It then restores the notification mode
# and starts swayidle (swayidle-startup.sh: unless jyoti is on).
# Unit files: systemd/.config/systemd/user/.

# Prevent idle timeouts when watching fullscreen videos
for_window [class=".*"] inhibit_idle fullscreen
for_window [app_id=".*"] inhibit_idle fullscreen

# No nm-applet/blueman-applet: Vyom's tarang (Wi-Fi) and setu (Bluetooth)
# cover them (WiFi secrets are stored by NetworkManager itself, psk-flags=0;
# bluez powers the adapter on by itself), so neither package is installed.
# Advanced network settings: nmtui.

# Battery Daemon: Warns at 20%, Critical at 10%, Forces Suspend at 5%.
# Systemd user service (systemd/.config/systemd/user/batsignal.service) rather
# than a raw exec: this had actually been silently broken this whole time --
# '-f LEVEL' is "battery FULL notification", not "force a command", and
# needed an argument it never got, so batsignal exited immediately on every
# launch. The real flag for "run a command at a level" is '-D COMMAND'.
# Restart=on-failure now too, so a future crash doesn't silently remove your
# only protection against an uncontrolled shutdown from battery depletion.
# (started by sway-session.sh, like the other session units)

# Clipboard history: cliphist@text / cliphist@image units (sway-session.sh).

include /etc/sway/config.d/*

# Theme: varna (Vayu's theme engine) writes the window colours, border width,
# gaps and corner radius here; the values above are the fallback without it.
# A glob, so a missing file is never an error.
include ~/.local/state/varna/sway*.conf


